# Host-installed node_modules and build output. Copying a macOS node_modules into the Linux web
# image would layer darwin-only native bindings over the freshly installed Linux ones, and `dist/`
# is regenerated inside the image anyway.
Web/node_modules/
Web/dist/
Web/.vite/

# The dev server's asset-pack destination (`/somnio-web`'s `SOMNIO_WEB_ASSET_DEST=Web/public/assets`).
# Vite copies `publicDir` verbatim into `dist/`, so without this line a developer who has run the
# dev loop bakes that pack into the image — while the Dockerfile's own pack step reads the build
# context's `assets/`, finds it empty, and logs "serving placeholders". The image then ships real
# art and reports the opposite, and the same commit yields different images depending on untracked
# local state. The pack reaches the image only through `assets/` + `bundle-web-assets.sh`, which is
# what enforces the UI-required/models-warn split. Scoped to `assets/` rather than all of
# `Web/public/` so a genuinely committed public file would still ship.
Web/public/assets/
